---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";

const sections = [
  {
    title: "1. Scope",
    body: "This Privacy Policy explains how SpacemanCodes LTD handles information when you use the Buff nutrition tracking app on iOS or Android, create a Buff account, use Buff's online services, or visit the Buff website.",
  },
  {
    title: "2. Information Buff handles",
    body: "Buff handles the information you choose to provide, including your name, email address, account credentials, meals, calories, macronutrients, recipes, goals, workouts, body measurements, progress photos, app preferences, meal photos and notes submitted for AI analysis, and support communications. Buff also processes device, app, security, and diagnostic information needed to authenticate requests, prevent abuse, and operate the service.",
  },
  {
    title: "3. Local storage and account sync",
    body: "Buff keeps your tracking data on your device. If you create or sign in to a Buff account, the records you choose to sync are also stored on Buff's servers so they can be restored, used across your devices, and made available to connected assistants you authorize. Account information, AI meal-analysis drafts and photos, and progress photos are stored on Buff's servers when you use those features.",
  },
  {
    title: "4. Apple Health and Health Connect",
    body: "If you connect Apple Health or Android Health Connect, Buff may read the workout and energy information you authorize so it can display and log activity in the app. Health permissions are controlled by your device settings and can be revoked at any time. Buff does not use health data for advertising or sell it.",
  },
  {
    title: "5. AI meal analysis",
    body: "When you request AI meal analysis, Buff sends the meal photos, notes, and follow-up corrections you provide to Buff's server and an AI service provider to generate a nutrition estimate. The estimate may be inaccurate and should be reviewed before you save it. Analysis drafts expire unless you confirm them; confirmed meal photos remain available with your saved meal until you delete the meal or your account.",
  },
  {
    title: "6. Food lookup and connected assistants",
    body: "When you scan a barcode or search for food, Buff sends the barcode or search terms needed to retrieve matching product information from food-data providers. If you connect a compatible AI assistant, it can access or change only the Buff data and actions you authorize, and you can revoke that connection in Buff settings.",
  },
  {
    title: "7. Subscriptions and RevenueCat",
    body: "Buff uses RevenueCat to manage Buff+ subscriptions purchased through Apple App Store or Google Play. Buff sends RevenueCat a server-generated pseudonymous customer identifier and receives purchase, product, entitlement, store, expiration, refund, and subscription-management metadata. RevenueCat does not receive your Buff password, meal log, meal photos, or health records from Buff. Apple or Google processes your payment information; Buff does not receive or store your full card details or store receipt tokens.",
  },
  {
    title: "8. Advertising, consent, and AdMob",
    body: "Buff shows Google AdMob banner ads only to users who are not entitled to Buff+. The Google Mobile Ads SDK and Google's User Messaging Platform may process an IP address (which can be used to estimate general location), device and advertising identifiers where available, app launches and ad interactions, and SDK diagnostic information for advertising, analytics, fraud prevention, and consent management. Google presents and stores privacy choices where required, and Buff provides an Ad privacy choices action in Settings when Google requires one. Buff requests non-personalized ads for users aged 13 to 17, users whose age is unavailable, and iOS users who deny or restrict tracking. Buff does not send AdMob your name, email address, Buff account or RevenueCat identifier, subscription metadata, meals, nutrition, workouts, body profile, photos, or health data.",
  },
  {
    title: "9. Service providers and website analytics",
    body: "Buff relies on service providers for hosting, authentication, email delivery, AI processing, food lookup, subscription management, and security. The Buff website uses privacy-focused aggregate analytics to understand page visits. These providers process information only as needed to supply their services and may operate in countries outside the United Kingdom, subject to their safeguards and applicable law.",
  },
  {
    title: "10. Retention and your controls",
    body: "You can edit or delete local records in Buff, disconnect health services or connected assistants, export your account data, and delete your Buff account from Settings. Account deletion removes the account and synced Buff data, but it does not cancel an App Store or Google Play subscription; cancel that separately through Manage Subscription before deleting the account. Store and payment providers may retain purchase records as required by law. Device backups may retain local data according to your platform settings.",
  },
  {
    title: "11. No sale of personal information",
    body: "SpacemanCodes LTD does not sell your personal information, nutrition log, body metrics, photos, health information, or purchase history.",
  },
  {
    title: "12. Changes to this policy",
    body: "We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The updated version will be identified by a new last updated date.",
  },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy - Buff"
  description="Privacy Policy for Buff on iOS and Android, including accounts, advertising, consent, health connections, and subscriptions."
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  summary="Last updated August 31, 2026. This policy explains what information Buff uses, where it is stored, when it is shared, and the controls available to you."
  contactIntro="For privacy questions, data requests, or account-deletion help, email "
  sections={sections}
/>
